      "side": 0,
      "message": "I think the stems from an STM32 requirement:\n\nAlignment check added to legacy stm32l flash driver: https://crrev.com/c/56627\n\nThe legacy [NPCX driver](https://crrev.com/c/233742) copied this check.\n\nThe legacy NPCX driver looks like it writes the data bytes one at time during program operations, so I don\u0027t see valid reason to restrict the source pointer to word alignment.\n\n```\n\tflash_execute_cmd(CMD_FLASH_PROGRAM, MASK_CMD_WR_ADR);\n\tfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n\t\tflash_execute_cmd(*data, MASK_CMD_WR_ONLY);\n\t\tdata++;\n\t}\n```\n\nNuvoton helped create the original Zephyr shim driver and copied the check here.",
